      "seed": 628507913,
      "version": 345,
      "versionNonce": 578530185,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1794909875424,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false
    },
    {
      "id": "4ZEd1fzPQGSoD8uFCyzf3",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 138.67919921875,
      "y": 936.6142578125,
      "width": 903.3994140625,
      "height": 225,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffc9c9",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0F",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 384918217,
      "version": 1147,
      "versionNonce": 1360550375,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1794909871920,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "A kernel launch is like one function call: main calls the kernel, the GPU runs it,\nand returns.\nDeclared inside the kernel: like a let inside a function. Gone when the launch ends.\nLives in global memory: stays on the card, so the next launch can read what this one wrote.\nExample: my image DeviceBuffer stays between launches; the kernel's row, col, and gray value\ndo not.\nRule of thumb: anything a later launch needs must be written to global memory before\nthe kernel ends since anything declared inside of the kernel or shared memory\ndoes not survive across launches.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "A kernel launch is like one function call: main calls the kernel, the GPU runs it,\nand returns.\nDeclared inside the kernel: like a let inside a function. Gone when the launch ends.\nLives in global memory: stays on the card, so the next launch can read what this one wrote.\nExample: my image DeviceBuffer stays between launches; the kernel's row, col, and gray value\ndo not.\nRule of thumb: anything a later launch needs must be written to global memory before\nthe kernel ends since anything declared inside of the kernel or shared memory\ndoes not survive across launches.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "cHOu_NGDb-F8tcdSYcYkL",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 422.3238313515625,
      "y": 1201.200191875,
      "width": 287.539794921875,
      "height": 25,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffc9c9",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
